# motrpac-human-presuspension-repro — single source of truth for the whole pipeline.
# Sourced by every stage script (scripts/lib/common.sh loads this).
#
# Two kinds of value live here, and they behave differently on purpose:
#
#   ${VAR:-default}   takes an inline override, e.g.  PARALLEL_CORES=8 make data
#                     (GITHUB_ROOT, RERUN_ATAC, PARALLEL_CORES,
#                      VARIANCEPARTITION_PARALLEL_CORES, EBAYES_LEGACY)
#                     EBAYES_LEGACY is overridable like the rest, and unlike the
#                     rest it moves results: it picks the eBayes estimator, so it
#                     changes every dream feature's moderated t and p.
#   VAR="literal"     is pinned. The assignment overwrites whatever the caller
#                     passed in, so an inline value is discarded.
#
# CURRENT_VERSION and NEW_VERSION are deliberately pinned. The release a run reads
# and the release it writes are decided here and nowhere else — change them by
# editing this file, not per-run, so a freeze cannot be built against one release
# while labelled with another. `CURRENT_VERSION=1.2 make sources` does NOT fetch
# v1.2; it fetches the pinned release and prints which one it used.
#
# The pipeline runs one way: every node runs, and consortium-gated inputs are a
# hard requirement. Preflight fails if the gated bucket is unreadable.

# ---- Versions --------------------------------------------------------------
CURRENT_VERSION="1.3"
# The incoming release. Files whose content changes this cycle are bumped to it; the
# per-file map in config/file_versions.json is where each file's version is decided,
# and this value is only the fallback for a file the map does not list. From v2.0 on
# that map covers every file in the collection, resources/ included — nothing ships
# unversioned any more.
NEW_VERSION="2.0"
# NOTE: NEW_VERSION is the FALLBACK, not a ceiling. The map decides each file's version and
# may put one past this value: the DA tables ship at v2.1, because they gained the
# CI.L_calculated/CI.R_calculated interval after 2.0 was cut. The collection directory is
# still c2.0 (PRODUCTION buckets below), so a v2.1 file lives inside the c2.0 tier. Bump
# this and NEW_PRODUCTION_BUCKET together if the collection itself is ever cut at 2.1.

# ---- Package versions ------------------------------------------------------
# The versions Stage 3 carry step 05 writes into the two TEST packages' DESCRIPTION.
# Passed explicitly because the step used to hardcode 2.0.0 for both, which was true
# when they sat at 0.0.1.101 and 0.2.4 and false once they were promoted past it: the
# step requires the requested version to be strictly ahead of the DESCRIPTION it finds,
# so a stale constant fails the stage rather than bumping it.
#
# These track what the repos currently hold (data 2.0.2, analysis 2.0.7). The data value
# is a patch bump carrying the prot-ph/prot-pr feature_metadata columns. The analysis value
# is NOT a bump: 2.0.6 and 2.0.7 were both promoted into that repo after this line was last
# edited, so the pinned 2.0.6 failed the step-05 check against a DESCRIPTION already ahead
# of it. It sits AT 2.0.7 because the whole 2.0 line is unmerged -- origin/main is 0.2.4 --
# so the pending HUMAN_FEATURE_TO_GENE carry corrects an unreleased artifact rather than
# earning a release of its own.
#
# THEY GO STALE THE SAME WAY. Once a test package is promoted into its repo, the repo
# carries this version and the next run fails the same check. Raise both here in the
# edit that promotes, or teach step 05 to derive the next patch from the DESCRIPTION.
export DATA_PKG_VERSION="${DATA_PKG_VERSION:-2.0.3}"
export ANALYSIS_PKG_VERSION="${ANALYSIS_PKG_VERSION:-2.0.7}"

# ---- Buckets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Production data hub (versioned) and the isolated staging root.
# The release directory is prefixed `c`, not `v` — the data hub renamed
# .../human-precovid-sed-adu/v1.3 to c1.3 on 2026-08-06. File names inside are
# unchanged and still carry their own _v<x.y> suffix.
PRODUCTION_BUCKET="gs://motrpac-data-hub/analysis/human-precovid-sed-adu/c${CURRENT_VERSION}"
NEW_PRODUCTION_BUCKET="gs://motrpac-data-hub/analysis/human-precovid-sed-adu/c${NEW_VERSION}"
STAGING_BUCKET="gs://pre-cawg/staging_20260806"
# Quant-id tier: raw post-quantification inputs the qc-norm stems read (cataloged by
# QUANTID_BUCKET_FILES.R into quantid_bucket_files.json). Versioned subdirs live under it.
QUANTID_BUCKET="gs://motrpac-data-hub/quant-id/human-precovid"

# ---- Repo paths ------------------------------------------------------------
# Resolved relative to this repo by default; override to point elsewhere.
# GITHUB_ROOT is the parent dir holding both in-scope repos.
#
# Taking the parent of PIPELINE_ROOT is right for a normal clone and wrong inside
# a linked git worktree, where PIPELINE_ROOT is .claude/worktrees/<name>/ and its
# parent holds other worktrees rather than the sibling repos. Resolve the main
# checkout first and take *its* parent, so a stage run from a worktree finds the
# same package repos as a run from the clone.
GITHUB_ROOT="${GITHUB_ROOT:-$(
  _common="$(git -C "${PIPELINE_ROOT}" rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir 2>/dev/null || true)"
  if [[ -n "${_common}" ]]; then cd "$(dirname "${_common}")/.." && pwd
  else cd "${PIPELINE_ROOT}/.." && pwd; fi
)}"
DATA_PKG_REPO="${GITHUB_ROOT}/MotrpacHumanPreSuspensionData"
ANALYSIS_PKG_REPO="${GITHUB_ROOT}/MotrpacHumanPreSuspensionAnalysis"

# This repo's root, exported so the R generators resolve their paths from one
# config env var instead of walking up parent dirs. Stage 1 writes build
# intermediates (freeze files) under ${PRECOVID_ROOT}/staging.
export PRECOVID_ROOT="${PIPELINE_ROOT}"
STAGING_DIR="${PRECOVID_ROOT}/staging"

# ---- Tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------
GSUTIL="gsutil"
GCLOUD="gcloud"
RSCRIPT="Rscript"

# ---- Rerun switches --------------------------------------------------------
# RERUN_ATAC — whether ATAC is rebuilt from raw or staged from the release.
#
# TRUE   step 06 generate_atac_qc_norm() fits voom/dream and writes the qc-norm matrix;
#        step 09 generate_atac_da() fits dream and writes the DA table.
# FALSE  both stems copy the released tables into the freeze verbatim, the way the
#        methylcap stems treat Yongchao Ge's externally produced files. Read from
#        06_generate_qc_norm/sources/atac_qc_norm/ and 09_build_da/sources/atac_da/.
#
# Feature and sample metadata are regenerated in BOTH modes. Only the qc-norm matrix
# and the DA table change hands. FALSE also drops step 09's dependency on the dream
# engine and on steps 05-08, since a file copy needs neither.
#
# FALSE requires the vendored files: make sources GROUPS="atac_qc_norm atac_da"
export RERUN_ATAC="${RERUN_ATAC:-TRUE}"

# EBAYES_LEGACY — which empirical-Bayes hyperparameter estimator eBayes uses, at the
# single call site in run_dream(). Governs every dream-based DA table.
#
# TRUE   limma's moment estimator, fitFDist(). What the v1.3 release was built with,
#        and what v2.0 ships, so the two remain comparable.
# FALSE  the profile-ML estimator fitFDistUnequalDF1(), which limma 3.62.0 introduced
#        and made the default whenever residual df are unequal across features.
#
# This has to be set explicitly because limma decides it for you otherwise, and its
# answer depends on the data: squeezeVar() resolves a NULL `legacy` as
# `identical(min(df), max(df))`, and dream gives every feature its own fractional
# residual df, so the condition is ALWAYS false and limma >= 3.62.0 silently takes the
# new estimator. Leaving it to the default is how v1.3 and v2.0 came to disagree.
#
# The estimator sets df.prior/s2.prior, which scale every feature's moderated variance
# and therefore its t and p — logFC is untouched. Measured on muscle metab-t-tca:
# df.prior 0.694 (TRUE) vs 2.000 (FALSE), s2.prior 7.16e-04 vs 2.96e-03. Features whose
# own variance sits near the prior scale move <1%; features far below it move a lot —
# cis-aconitate t by 1.41x, adipose cis-aconitate by 3.59x. The effect grows as the
# residual df shrinks, so plasma (rdf ~686) barely moves and muscle/adipose (rdf
# ~130-270) move most. Only the methylcap tables are outside this: they are external
# MALAX GLMM output copied verbatim and never touch dream.
#
# TRUE is chosen for continuity with v1.3, not because it is the better estimator.
# fitFDistUnequalDF1 is what limma now recommends for exactly the unequal-fractional-df
# case dream creates; revisit this when the collection can absorb the change.
export EBAYES_LEGACY="${EBAYES_LEGACY:-TRUE}"

# RUN_SCION — whether step 16 infers the SCION networks.
#
# TRUE   both networks are inferred, per exercise group, into staging/scion/.
# FALSE  the step exits 77 and 10_build_data.sh records it SKIP.
#
# On by default: `make all` runs every step, and a step is opted out of rather than into.
# This is the one step measured in hours to days — a random-forest fit per cluster per
# group per network. Submit it with EXECUTOR=slurm rather than running it inline.
export RUN_SCION="${RUN_SCION:-TRUE}"

# Null replicates inferred after the observed network, per network per group. 0 infers the
# observed network only, which is what the figure is drawn from. The networks are too dense
# for a permutation null to be the boundary, so edges are cut by a stricter weight cutoff
# instead. Raising this is the difference between one fit and hours to days of them.
export SCION_PERMUTATIONS="${SCION_PERMUTATIONS:-0}"

# Cores handed to run_SCION(). It parallelises the per-target random forests over
# num.cores - 1 workers, and only when num.cores > 2.
export SCION_CORES="${SCION_CORES:-11}"

# Re-infer runs that already have a network table on disk. On, so re-entering the step
# restarts rather than resumes; SCION_FORCE=FALSE resumes.
export SCION_FORCE="${SCION_FORCE:-TRUE}"

# ---- Parallelization -------------------------------------------------------
# Two switches, split by library, because one of the two libraries is broken in parallel.
#
# PARALLEL_CORES — mice imputation only (prot-pr/ph imputed, via mice::futuremice).
# 1 = serial. Default leaves 2 cores free on this 12-core host.
#
# mice is safe in parallel and measured to be so: futuremice() parallelises over the m
# IMPUTATIONS, not over features, so each worker imputes the whole matrix and no worker owns
# a subset of features. Serial and parallel returned identical feature counts at 5, 10, 20
# and 100 features. (Worker count is bounded by m — with m = 3 only 3 workers engage.)
export PARALLEL_CORES="${PARALLEL_CORES:-10}"

# VARIANCEPARTITION_PARALLEL_CORES — every variancePartition path.
# Read by variancepartition_parallel_enabled() in 10_build_data/lib/qc_helpers.R, which
# governs both consumers:
#   step 06  generate_atac_qc_norm()  voomWithDreamWeights(..., BPPARAM)
#   step 09  run_dream()              dream(..., BPPARAM)   [all DA stems]
#
# BACKEND: MulticoreParam (fork) at BOTH call sites as of this branch. It was SnowParam SOCK,
# and SOCK is what the measurements below indict — not parallelism as such. SnowParam's default
# exportglobals = TRUE copies the manager's options() into every worker, and `warn` is not on
# BiocParallel's blocklist, so each worker inherits the options(warn = 2) that
# variancePartition:::run_lmm sets before bpiterate(). A SOCK worker is a cold R session, so the
# first findbars() it evaluates fires lme4 1.1-38's once-per-session reformulas deprecation
# warning, warn = 2 turns that into an error, and run_lmm_on_batch's bptry drops that one
# feature. MulticoreParam forks, so every worker inherits an already-armed warning cache and the
# warning never fires again.
#
# WHY 8 and not detectCores() - 2 = 10: this host has 12 logical but 8 PERFORMANCE cores, and
# fork workers are copy-on-write over a parent that reaches ~4 GB on ATAC, so 10 workers both
# oversubscribe the fast cores and crowd 32 GB of RAM. 8 keeps every worker on a performance
# core. Raise it only after watching memory on a full ATAC fit.
#
# The SOCK measurements, kept because they are why this must never go back to SnowParam.
# Measured on this 12-core host (detectCores()-2 = 10 workers): SOCK SILENTLY LOSES EXACTLY ONE
# FEATURE PER WORKER.
#
#   dream, adipose prot-pr    1 core   7056 features   172s   == the released count
#                            10 cores  7046 features    42s   10 lost, nothing logged
#   voom, muscle ATAC        1 core     100 features
#                            10 cores    90 features           10 lost
#                            1 core      20 / 10 / 5 / 3 features   all fine
#                            10 cores    20 -> 10, then ERROR below 20
#
# Mechanism: variancePartition calls lme4::findbars()/nobars(), which lme4 1.1-38 deprecated
# in favour of the reformulas package and warns about ONCE PER SESSION. Every SOCK worker is
# a fresh session, so each one hits that warning on the first feature it touches, the worker
# converts the warning to an error, and that model fails. One dead feature per worker.
#
# So the loss scales with worker count, not data size: 10 workers costs 10 features whether
# the matrix holds 7000 or 20. Where a stem has fewer features than workers every feature is
# some worker's first and the whole fit dies — prot-clinical (3 analytes) errors with
# "All models failed", and ATAC voom errors at 10 features or fewer.
#
# NOT about missing values: 9 of the 10 features lost on adipose prot-pr have zero NAs.
# NOT fixed by upgrading — variancePartition 1.39.5 completes the reformulas migration and
# still loses exactly 10. NOT the same problem as the variancePartition 1.38.1 + lme4 1.1-38
# pin, which is what lets dream fit NA-carrying features at all (under lme4 2.0 every one is
# dropped even serially) — that pin is still required, independent of the backend.
#
# Both call sites are guarded: generate_atac_qc_norm() and run_mice() compare feature counts
# in against out and stop rather than ship a short matrix. The guards stay under fork — they
# are what would catch a regression here.
#
# Still verify DA row counts against the release after a parallel run.
export VARIANCEPARTITION_PARALLEL_CORES="${VARIANCEPARTITION_PARALLEL_CORES:-8}"
